# The `show` tool: std/githist-lib (std/bash with the shared history library
# bound) with this directory's command body curried onto it, plus the `help` an
# agent registers it by.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, like std/caos-test's, so they live here rather
# than in the worker -- and a `.caos-expr` is STRIPPED from the tree it is
# evaluated against, so rewording them re-keys this tool's arg tree and nothing
# it builds.
#
# `@git` is what asks the launch for the workspace commit (`wc`) and the turn's
# ref snapshot (`refs`). Only `@git` tools get them: `wc` moves every step, so
# binding it into a build or test tool would sink that tool's cache.
HELP=<<END
Show one commit: its hash, parents, author, full message, and the unified diff it introduced (against its first parent). Optionally scope the diff to a path.
@param [rev] The commit to show (default HEAD, the current workspace). A commit hash, a snapshot ref, or HEAD~N / ref^.
@param [path] Restrict the shown diff to this workspace-relative path.
@git
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/githist-lib --worker1:@=worker.sh --help=$HELP
